WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:13.680
We might not notice it, but the world, is
changing really fast: &nbsp;

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:25.640
Biotechnology, robotics, nanotechnology…every
day, somewhere on Earth, some discovery is

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.869
being made.

00:00:26.869 --> 00:00:31.240
Discoveries which will make our lives longer,
more comfortable, and generally much better.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.900
&nbsp;
We could almost say, dear viewer, that we

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:37.059
are on board a high speed train bound for
the future.

00:00:37.059 --> 00:00:42.590
There are already incredible companies today,
which look like they could have come out of

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:45.220
a science fiction movie: Want to have some
examples?

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.220
Well then...

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:47.220
Are you familiar with Organovo?

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:49.339
It is a truly incredible company.

00:00:49.339 --> 00:00:54.119
It’s listed on the NASDAQ and its business
is no less than the bioprinting of tissues

00:00:54.119 --> 00:00:58.890
to implant in the human body and thus, eliminating
the need for organ transplants.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:01.200
Can you imagine printing a liver?

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.350
It’s remarkable stuff.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.690
And what about the company Modern Meadow?

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:11.299
This start-up’s aim is to produce leather
and meat without having to kill any animals.

00:01:11.299 --> 00:01:17.979
They want to produce their own steaks in a
lab and take them to the supermarkets.

00:01:17.979 --> 00:01:20.410
The big question is though: Would you eat
it?

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:22.609
And another example, have you heard of Illumina?

00:01:22.609 --> 00:01:26.999
It is the largest company dedicated to DNA
sequencing.

00:01:26.999 --> 00:01:31.990
Among other targets, they are trying to detect
cancer before any of the symptoms appear.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:38.939
Almost unbelievable, isn't it?Well, these
are only three of the hundreds of companies

00:01:38.939 --> 00:01:41.250
which are literally building the future today.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.600
But, you know what?

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.359
Organ printing, DNA sequencing…

00:01:44.359 --> 00:01:49.429
That’s not the best part, the best is that
the end of poverty is getting closer every

00:01:49.429 --> 00:01:52.979
day, and the reality is that it’s already
right around the corner.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:55.740
And, listen, we aren't just talking about
extreme poverty here.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:02:00.380
On the contrary, current realities like hunger
or not being able to eat meat or not having

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:04.729
access to health care - or even not being
able to go on holiday - are going to be rare,

00:02:04.729 --> 00:02:06.950
very infrequent in fact.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:11.680
And this is going to be a reality in probably
just a few years.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:20.150
Alright, alright, now some of you might be
thinking: Simon´s lost it!

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.420
It’s all downhill for Visual Politik from
here...

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.800
Well, no, I haven't actually lost my mind.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:29.080
In fact, here, with all of you as witnesses,
I am willing to bet you that in the next year

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:33.950
we will experience the best period of prosperity
in the history of mankind...

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.500
And I am not the only one sharing this opinion.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:43.830
Listen to what Warren Buffet, the investment
genius, has to say about it:

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.710
Or Barack Obama, as well:

00:02:45.710 --> 00:03:05.010
Well, I am here to tell you 
even more.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:09.920
This wave of prosperity will bring opportunities
we had never even thought of before.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:20.180
But, alright, for the sceptics, here are the
numbers:

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:25.770
It is estimated that, by the end of 2016,
3.2 billion people are going to already belong

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:31.340
to the middle class, and each year, more than
140 million people will make it into this

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:33.320
‘select club’.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:38.320
It is as if every year a group of people,
the size of the population of Mexico, are

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:39.530
leaving poverty behind.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:44.000
Note here that this process is accelerating
and it’s expected that by 2020, that’s

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.130
just 3 years from the time this video going
out, most part of the world’s population

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:52.030
will belong to the middle class.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:58.070
This growth middle class will mean that the
poor will be in the minority.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:06.090
But… before we continue, I am sure your
might be wondering: how exactly do you define

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:07.320
the middle class?

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:11.600
Since income levels vary country to country,
when we talk about middle class we are talking

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:16.720
about people who can afford to have a varied
diet, people who can face and cover unexpected

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:20.530
expenses and education, and people who can
buy an automobile.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:25.110
These people might not be rich, but they definitely
aren't poor any more.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:30.229
And this is a new thing in the history of
mankind.

00:04:30.229 --> 00:04:36.860
So now that you have an idea of how things
are changing today let’s have a look at

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:38.580
the historical perspective:

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:42.600
When Napoleon was fighting everyone in Europe,
only 2 million people could be considered

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:43.689
middle class.

00:04:43.689 --> 00:04:46.810
That is less than half the population of Singapore
today.

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:51.050
A pretty tough situation for the vast majority
of people living at that time…

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:56.690
Well, since then, 150 years have passed, but
it wasn’t until the 1970s that the number

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:02.690
of people in the middle class passed the 1
billion people mark.

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:09.560
Today, the number is about 3 billion and,
by 2021, it is expected to reach 4 billion.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:15.479
And as I mentioned the process is getting
faster and faster every day.

00:05:15.479 --> 00:05:19.009
And this new middle class are going to make
an impressive entrance.

00:05:19.009 --> 00:05:23.210
Don't believe me?

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:47.520
Yep, the city you are 

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:52.509
looking at is Hanoi, the capital city of Vietnam,
the country in the world where capitalism

00:05:52.509 --> 00:05:59.310
is most liked - that’s according to a recent
study from the Pew Research Center.

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:02.469
Seems like we in the West might have some
catching up to do.

00:06:02.469 --> 00:06:08.620
In fact, the majority of this new middle class
are coming from Asia.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:18.689
Almost 9 out of 10 new people who make it
to the middle class live in Asia, the continent

00:06:18.689 --> 00:06:22.650
of the economic booms, and the growing epicentre
of power on Earth.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:25.749
You just have to take a look at countries
like the Philippines or Thailand.

00:06:25.749 --> 00:06:30.270
In just a few years, these countries’ middle
classes will be as big as those in the UK,

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:31.300
France and Italy.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:35.779
Yes, they will remain poorer countries, but
the growth of the middle class is still very

00:06:35.779 --> 00:06:36.779
impressive!

00:06:36.779 --> 00:06:39.639
But do you want to know how things are really
changing?

00:06:39.639 --> 00:06:42.370
Well, this is Jakarta…

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:51.229
And think about what this means for the companies!

00:06:51.229 --> 00:06:53.250
But that’s something we’re going to look
into later…

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:57.830
However, of all these countries, one is making
a big difference: And that’s China, whose

00:06:57.830 --> 00:07:00.979
middle class has exploded.

00:07:00.979 --> 00:07:05.650
According to the estimations by McKinsey analysts,
if in 5 years this amount of people were to

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:09.990
create, say, the Chinese Republic of Middle
Class Citizens, this country would be the

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:13.280
third most populated country in the world.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.360
Not bad, ayy?

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:19.409
So if you want to know what these changes
really mean, take a look at Chongqing, the

00:07:19.409 --> 00:07:29.630
most populated city in China:

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:33.139
Because of the growth of the middle class,
these people now have money available to buy

00:07:33.139 --> 00:07:38.120
all kinds of products: clothing, electronics,
cars, and, of course, travel.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:43.070
And, now you can probably understand why the
countries in Asia, especially China, are so

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:46.190
important for multinational companies.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:56.759
Pay attention to 
this data, because it may be interesting if

00:07:56.759 --> 00:07:58.280
you are thinking about starting a business:

00:07:58.280 --> 00:08:02.580
It is estimated that the spending growth of
the Chinese in the next four years alone,

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:05.080
will exceed what the British or Germans spend.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:09.979
So, if you, our VisualPolitik friends, have
a company, you might want to think about investigating

00:08:09.979 --> 00:08:16.520
the Asian market, because many opportunities
will appear in the next few years.

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:25.219
But the consequences of all this aren't just
an opportunity to make money and to do more

00:08:25.219 --> 00:08:26.219
business.

00:08:26.219 --> 00:08:29.779
Probably, the most important consequence of
all this middle class expansion is that we

00:08:29.779 --> 00:08:31.650
will live in a happier world.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:32.800
Let me explain…

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.419
You’ve probably heard the phrase: “Money
doesn't make you happy”?

00:08:35.419 --> 00:08:39.669
Well, actually according to recent research,
that is not entirely true.

00:08:39.669 --> 00:08:44.339
In 2010, Angus Deaton and Daniel Kahneman,
both winners of the Nobel Prizes in Economics,

00:08:44.339 --> 00:08:49.459
presented a paper which proved that up to
the figure of $75,000 dollars a year, happiness

00:08:49.459 --> 00:08:52.140
and income were very closely related.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:56.430
Meaning, more income equals more happiness
(up to $75,000 a year).

00:08:56.430 --> 00:09:00.300
It makes sense, with more money you don't
have to worry about making it to the end of

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:03.899
the month, paying your bills, not having enough
to eat, not being able to take your family

00:09:03.899 --> 00:09:05.880
to the doctor etc etc.

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:09.990
So, according to these two academics, the
expansion of the middle class is leading towards

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:11.110
a happier world.

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:13.350
But wait, there’s more…

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:18.121
More middle class means more educated people,
more researchers, more entrepreneurs, more

00:09:18.121 --> 00:09:21.720
ideas, more innovation and, therefore, more
progress.

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:26.320
Well, today in China, there are more college
students than in the United States.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:28.790
Remember the companies we saw at the beginning
of the video?

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:32.760
Well, soon enough there are going to be plenty
more of those.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:40.350
Now, you may be wondering: if it is all as
wonderful as they are describing at VisualPolitik…

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:44.149
How come people such as Donald Trump and Le
Pen are so popular?

00:09:44.149 --> 00:09:48.170
Well, this middle class boom is not happening
in all parts of the world.

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:52.450
Therefore it is important we understand that
if the Western economies aren´t working perfectly

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:58.220
or are having problems, they should take responsibility
for it and stop blaming it on the other countries.

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:03.500
There are plenty of opportunities in the global
economy and now is the time to adapt and seize

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:04.500
them.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:08.230
But, I can guess what you’re thinking: is
all of this growth really sustainable?

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:11.480
Won’t all this progress and development
destroy the environment?

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:13.370
Or cause other problems.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:17.550
Well, that’s not very clear.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:25.949
Now it is true that in theory, more middle
class means more spending and, therefore,

00:10:25.949 --> 00:10:30.319
more consumerism, more pressure on natural
resources etc… but there are some things

00:10:30.319 --> 00:10:31.320
to consider:

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:35.610
First: more middle class also means more people
in big cities, and the consumerism here is

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.529
usually more sustainable.

00:10:37.529 --> 00:10:42.070
Transport is the most evident example: While
public transport is frequent in large cities,

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:47.350
it is rare in small places.More middle class
also means faster demographic transition,

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:51.029
so more women study and work so the population
tends to shrink as well.

00:10:51.029 --> 00:10:55.990
And, above all, more middle class means, as
we said before, more ideas and more innovation

00:10:55.990 --> 00:11:00.149
and, among these, are often ideas which allow
more sustainable consumerism.

00:11:00.149 --> 00:11:04.980
So, however we want to approach the situation,
and although there certainly a lot of room

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:06.779
for advancement and improvement…

00:11:06.779 --> 00:11:11.089
We think that this is really a time in history
where we should be feeling rather positive.

00:11:11.089 --> 00:11:15.329
But, that’s our opinion here at Visual Politik,
but what do you think?

00:11:15.329 --> 00:11:17.709
Do you believe we are moving towards a better
world?

00:11:17.709 --> 00:11:21.810
Do you think Asia can be a land of opportunity
and business?

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:23.060
Let us know in the comments below!

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:24.920
We’d love to hear your thoughts.

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:28.839
And if you enjoyed this video please hit that
thumbs up button below, and don’t forget

00:11:28.839 --> 00:11:31.740
to subscribe for brand new videos every Monday
and Thursday.

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:34.560
And, as always, I’ll see you in the next
video.

